    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, keeping each piece of logic in its proper layer:\n\n- **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** \u2014 now formats `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` from `(city, lastName, cityOwnerCount)`, with a shared private `abbreviate(...)` helper for the two 3-letter prefixes (no duplication). The `NNNN` is `cityOwnerCount + 1`.\n- **Repository layer** \u2014 added `countByCity(String city)` (case-insensitive) to `OwnerRepository` and all three implementations (`JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `SpringDataOwnerRepository`), mirroring the existing `countByName` pattern.\n- **Service layer** \u2014 added `countOwnersInCity(String city)` to `ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`, delegating to the repository.\n- **Controller** \u2014 `addOwner` now generates the code from the owner's city, last name, and the per-city owner count.\n\nThe **membership number** is derived in `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` from `customerCode` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format without any change there \u2014 the derivation stays in one place.\n\nEverything compiles and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the new acceptance assertion that `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`.",
